==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|theosophia|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|θεοσοφία||knowledge of things divine|lang=grc|tr=thesophia}}, from {{term|θεός||god|tr=theos|lang=grc}} + {{term|σοφία||wisdom|tr=sophia|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-|theosophies}}

# {{religion}} any doctrine of religious philosophy and mysticism claiming that knowledge of [[God]] can be attained through [[mystical]] [[insight]] and spiritual ecstasy, and that direct communication with the [[transcendent]] world is possible.

====Derived terms====
* [[theosophic]]
* [[theosophist]]

